          253,
          80,
          1235,
          955,
          1505
        ]
      ],
      "en": "Let $X$ be the space of sequences $x=\\{x_1,x_2,x_3,\\ldots\\}$ with only finitely many nonzero terms and norm\\[\\|x\\|:=\\sup_{i\\in\\mathbb{N}}|x_i|.\\]Let $T:X\\to X$ be defined by\\[Tx:=\\left\\{x_1,\\dfrac{x_2}{2},\\dfrac{x_3}{3},\\ldots\\right\\}.\\]Show that $T$ is linear and bounded but that $T^{-1}$ is unbounded. Why does this not contradict the bounded inverse theorem?",
      "zh": "设 $X$ 为仅有有限个非零项的序列 $x=\\{x_1,x_2,x_3,\\ldots\\}$ 所组成的空间, 范数为\\[\\|x\\|:=\\sup_{i\\in\\mathbb{N}}|x_i|.\\]用下式定义 $T:X\\to X$:\\[Tx:=\\left\\{x_1,\\dfrac{x_2}{2},\\dfrac{x_3}{3},\\ldots\\right\\}.\\]证明 $T$ 线性且有界, 但 $T^{-1}$ 无界. 为什么这不与有界逆定理矛盾?",
      "label": "ex:incomplete-finite-sequence-bounded-inverse-counterexample",
